CORE
main.cpp
--winx64 --cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ 5 is a digit: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ a is not a digit: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ a is alpha: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ newline is space: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ z is not upper: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.6\] line \d+ comma is punct: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.7\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
The classic ctype<char> model knew only libstdc++'s _M_table and glibc's
mask encoding; the MSVC STL's _Ctype._Table and enumerator masks were not
modelled, and locale::_Init (in the runtime library) had no body.
